# Deploy target for deploy/deploy.sh.
# Copy this file to deploy/config.env (which is gitignored) and set your values.
#
#   cp deploy/config.env.example deploy/config.env
#   # then edit deploy/config.env
#
# DEPLOY_SERVER       — SSH destination with passwordless (key-based) access.
# DEPLOY_DIR          — the Shiny Server app directory on that host.
# DEPLOY_LIBRARY_ROOT — ABSOLUTE path to a local SESPy library checkout at the
#                       tag this app's pyproject.toml pins (e.g. v1.18.0), with
#                       a clean working tree; the deploy aborts otherwise. Its
#                       sespy/ is vendored as $DEPLOY_DIR/sespy, and its
#                       tests/parity/check_live.py runs the live pre-flight.
#                       A non-empty DEPLOY_LIBRARY_ROOT in the environment wins
#                       over this file (for a one-run rollback, below).

DEPLOY_SERVER=user@host
DEPLOY_DIR=/srv/shiny-server/SESPy
DEPLOY_LIBRARY_ROOT=/abs/path/SESPy

# Optional:
# DEPLOY_MOSAIC_DIR — MosaicSES app dir on the same server (it symlinks this
#                     app's sespy/ and sespy_app/); its restart.txt is touched
#                     after a deploy.
# DEPLOY_REPO_ROOT  — deploy another sespy-app checkout with this script
#                     (rollback: a worktree of an older app tag, run with
#                     --rollback, plus DEPLOY_LIBRARY_ROOT at the library tag
#                     that older app pins). Use ABSOLUTE paths (a relative one
#                     resolves against your current directory). Do NOT leave
#                     it set in this file: pass both on the command line for
#                     the one rollback run, or every normal deploy will ship
#                     that tree:
#                       DEPLOY_REPO_ROOT=/abs/path/sespy-app-rollback \
#                       DEPLOY_LIBRARY_ROOT=/abs/path/sespy-lib-rollback \
#                         deploy/deploy.sh --rollback
# DEPLOY_SUDO_TEST  — 1 = check live-file readability with `sudo -n -u shiny`
#                     (a denied sudo can raise auth alerts; default is stat).
#
# DEPLOY_MOSAIC_DIR=/srv/shiny-server/MosaicSES
# DEPLOY_SUDO_TEST=1
